    aiContent: {
      difficulty: 'Intermediate',
      considerations: [
        'Win the pot by having the best five-card poker hand at showdown as a partnership, or by being the last partnership with a member still in the hand. If one member of the winning partnership folded, the remaining partner wins the whole pot.',
        'After ante and deal, all players roll one card simultaneously. Partner selection proceeds by rank of the exposed card: highest picks first, then highest unpartnered, until all are paired. Each partnership combines their eight remaining cards and selects three to use with their two upcards to form a five-card hand. There are three betting rounds; after each round one of the three chosen cards is turned face up. Partners play as a team but bet as individuals: if one folds the other may continue. At showdown the team with the highest hand shares the pot; if one partner folded, the other wins the whole pot.',
        'Even number of players only. Everyone antes and is dealt five cards face down.',
        'Roll is simultaneous: everyone selects and exposes one card at once.',
      ],
    },
